{"change_summary":"Addressed both pending amendments. The TUI integer-count regression now selects `ActionKind::AddShrimp` by kind instead of relying on a brittle action index, and schema v4→v5 save migration now maps legacy `TrimPlants` queued actions to `TrimPlantsAndLeaveCuttings` so old saves preserve the original in-tank cuttings behavior. I also updated the migration comments and renamed the save-load regression to reflect the preserved semantics.","outstanding_risks":[],"steps":[{"description":"Inspected the pending amendments in the TUI action form tests and the schema v4→v5 save migration to confirm the exact failure modes and required behavior.","order":0,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Updated `crates/tank_tui/src/screens/actions.rs` so the integer-count test navigates to `AddShrimp` by matching `ActionKind` rather than a hard-coded position in `ActionKind::ALL`.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Updated `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs` so legacy `TrimPlants` queued actions migrate to `TrimPlantsAndLeaveCuttings`, and revised the migration documentation to state that legacy closed-system semantics are preserved.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Updated `crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs` so the legacy schema v4 migration regression asserts `TrimPlantsAndLeaveCuttings` after load and uses a test name that reflects semantic preservation.","order":3,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Ran formatting and validation across the touched packages to confirm both amendments and surrounding trim/save behavior remain green.","order":4,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all` completed successfully.","`cargo test -p tank_tui` passed (3 tests).","`cargo test -p tank_core --test save_load` passed (21 tests), including `legacy_schema_v4_saves_preserve_trim_plants_as_leave_cuttings`.","`cargo test -p tank_core` passed for the full package suite, including trim/export, budget tracking, and save migration coverage."]}